    "date": "2026-10-18",
    "body": "Mareader has its own icon: an open book whose edges draw an M, with one\nline highlighted. This release also gathers everything since v0.0.1.\n\n## What's new\n\n- **Dictionary page.** A Dictionary button in the Library and reader title\n  bars, or Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+D, opens a full dictionary: every pack or one,\n  Languages mode from one language to another (bridged through English\n  when no pack joins them), close matches, recent searches and the\n  keyboard throughout.\n- **Floating dictionary.** In the reader it floats over the page instead:\n  move it, resize it, fold it to a small pill that shows the word and its\n  answer, or open it as a page. While it's open, Look up answers in it and\n  the selection stays. Settings › Dictionary › In the reader can choose\n  the full page instead.\n- **Notes and bookmarks.** Write a note on any highlight; a Notes panel\n  lists them by chapter, with search. Bookmark pages. Export highlights\n  and notes, and restyle one highlight or several at once.\n- **A rebuilt Library.** A home-screen grid you arrange by dragging, with\n  shelves you make by stacking books, multi-select, a list view, watched\n  folders with a single import form, links and duplicates, and a compact\n  way to remove books.\n- **Reading.** Grab empty space to pan the pages; hold a pane to lift and\n  move it; open pictures large with a double click; footnotes open in\n  place; reopen recent books from an empty pane.\n- **Look and feel.** A compact, foldable Appearance popover; a keyboard\n  shortcut sheet; a redesigned lookup card that points at its word;\n  Burmese and other complex scripts shaped in every panel; small text\n  kept readable on every paper.\n- **AI.** Models refresh and fetch on their own; one download fetches the\n  word-level data, with options after.\n\n## Which file to download\n\n| System | File | Install |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| macOS 11 or later, Apple silicon | `Mareader_0.0.2_aarch64.dmg` | open it and drag Mareader to Applications |\n| macOS 11 or later, Intel | `Mareader_0.0.2_x64.dmg` | the same |\n| Windows 10 or 11 | `mareader_0.0.2_x64-setup.exe` | run it; it installs for you alone, no administrator needed |\n| Windows, managed machines | `mareader_0.0.2_x64_en-US.msi` | `msiexec /i` it, or deploy it as usual |\n| Debian, Ubuntu, Mint, Pop!_OS | `mareader_0.0.2_amd64.deb` | `sudo apt install ./mareader_0.0.2_amd64.deb` |\n| Arch and its family | `mareader_0.0.2_x86_64.tar.gz` and `PKGBUILD` | put both in one folder, then `makepkg -si` |\n| Any other Linux (glibc 2.35 or newer) | `mareader_0.0.2_x86_64.AppImage` | `chmod +x` it, then run it |\n\nInstalling over v0.0.1 keeps your library, settings and highlights.\n`SHA256SUMS` lists every file's checksum: `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS\n--ignore-missing` on Linux, `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing`\non a Mac.\n\n## The first launch\n\nThis build is not signed by Apple or Microsoft yet, so each system asks\nonce:\n\n- **macOS:** \"Apple could not verify Mareader\". Choose Done, then open\n  System Settings › Privacy & Security and choose Open Anyway next to\n  Mareader. Later launches open directly.\n- **Windows:** \"Windows protected your PC\". Choose More info, then Run\n  anyway.\n- **Linux:** nothing to approve. The AppImage only needs to be executable.\n\nmacOS and Windows may keep showing the old icon for a while, as they\ncache icons; it updates after a restart or once the cache refreshes.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- Apple Intelligence needs a Mac with Apple silicon and macOS 26.\n- Your library stays on this computer; syncing between machines comes in\n  a later release.\n- Linux packages are for x86_64 only; ARM Linux and Windows on ARM have\n  no build yet.\n\nBefore publishing, CI built every installer on its own system, then\ninstalled each one, opened a book with it and removed it again.\n",
