    "body": "The first build of Mareader for macOS, Windows and Linux: a calm reader\nfor PDF, EPUB, plain text and Markdown, native (egui and wgpu, no webview).\n\nInside: single, spread, vertical and horizontal page views; every\ntypography setting for books; up to four panes, each with its own theme;\nlight, dark and dim papers with tints, textures and grain; a library with\nshelves and watched folders; highlights, gloss cards, offline dictionaries,\nCEFR word levels and Explain through Apple Intelligence or the AI provider\nyou choose; search in both formats; and full keyboard control.\n\n## Which file to download\n\n| System | File | Install |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| macOS 11 or later, Apple silicon | `Mareader_0.0.1_aarch64.dmg` | open it and drag Mareader to Applications |\n| macOS 11 or later, Intel | `Mareader_0.0.1_x64.dmg` | the same |\n| Windows 10 or 11 | `mareader_0.0.1_x64-setup.exe` | run it; it installs for you alone, no administrator needed |\n| Windows, managed machines | `mareader_0.0.1_x64_en-US.msi` | `msiexec /i` it, or deploy it as usual |\n| Debian, Ubuntu, Mint, Pop!_OS | `mareader_0.0.1_amd64.deb` | `sudo apt install ./mareader_0.0.1_amd64.deb` |\n| Arch and its family | `mareader_0.0.1_x86_64.tar.gz` and `PKGBUILD` | put both in one folder, then `makepkg -si` |\n| Any other Linux (glibc 2.35 or newer) | `mareader_0.0.1_x86_64.AppImage` | `chmod +x` it, then run it |\n\nEach installer opens PDF, EPUB, text (`.txt`, `.text`) and Markdown\n(`.md`, `.markdown`, `.mdown`) files from your file manager. `SHA256SUMS`\nlists every file's checksum: `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing`\non Linux, `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing` on a Mac.\n\n## The first launch\n\nThis build is not signed by Apple or Microsoft yet, so each system asks\nonce:\n\n- **macOS:** \"Apple could not verify Mareader\". Choose Done, then open\n  System Settings › Privacy & Security and choose Open Anyway next to\n  Mareader. Later launches open directly.\n- **Windows:** \"Windows protected your PC\". Choose More info, then Run\n  anyway.\n- **Linux:** nothing to approve. The AppImage only needs to be executable.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- On Windows, the setup makes Mareader open PDF, EPUB, text and Markdown\n  files unless you already chose another app for them; `.txt` files\n  then open in Mareader rather than Notepad. Uninstalling restores them.\n- Apple Intelligence needs a Mac with Apple silicon and macOS 26.\n- Your library stays on this computer; syncing between machines comes in\n  a later release.\n- Linux packages are for x86_64 only; ARM Linux and Windows on ARM have\n  no build yet.\n\nBefore publishing, CI built every installer on its own system, then\ninstalled each one, opened a book with it and removed it again. The Arch\npackage is the exception: CI checks its contents and `PKGBUILD`, as no\nArch runner exists.\n",
